By default, most users should use aero-omni5.xml or aero-omni7.xml.
The former has 1 generic wireless MANET and 1 EMANE MANET, and the
latter has 2 generic wireless MANETs. Other *.xmls are in various
stages of development and included as-is with no guarantee of
suitability for any purpose.

When a model is runing in core-gui, double-clicking on any of the
node icons will bring up a terminal window on that node. IPv4 and
NATs are used in the Internetworking underlay, while IPv6 is used
in the MANETs and Internetworking overlay. Standard commands for
testing include: "ping6", "ip -6 ro sh", "ssh" and any other
IPv6-enabled application. "ifconfig omni0" shows the overlay
multilink network interface.

Currently, all Clients can ping6 each other over the overlay while
nodes in MANETs can only ping6 other nodes within the same MANET.
A node in a source MANET can ssh into its connected Client, then
ssh from there into the target Client and then onto a node in the
target MANET, but this is application-layer proxying and does not
represent true MANET Internetworking. Goal is to get nodes in
source MANET to ping6 nodes in target MANET through segment
traversal of the Internetworking overlay (to be included in
future releases).
